# CITATION.cff -- how to cite sremu (WP12). Citation File Format 1.2.0.
#
# LICENCE PENDING: the licence is an open administrative gate (DESIGN 2.1, RQ-100, human
# gate H-2; see LICENSE-PENDING.md). CFF's `license` key accepts SPDX identifiers only, so it
# is omitted on purpose until all six authors and IIT Bhilai agree; pyproject.toml declares
# LicenseRef-Pending meanwhile.
# At the first public tagged release add: license, repository-code, date-released, the
# Zenodo DOI (RQ-101), ORCIDs, and a preferred-citation pointing to the arXiv preprint.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use sremu, please cite it using the metadata below. sremu is pre-release software;
  its licence has not been chosen yet (see LICENSE-PENDING.md).
type: software
title: "sremu: Smart Radio Environment EMUlator"
version: 0.1.0.dev0
abstract: >-
  sremu is a software-only, IQ-level radio-environment emulator for reconfigurable
  intelligent surfaces (RIS). RIS configurations are timestamped runtime commands from an
  external controller, applied at an exact, logged sample on every receiver; per-state RIS
  responses can be imported from measurements; wall-clock behaviour is measured and
  reported.
